WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.667
Charge cards on file, one or many, and log a declined card.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:10.567
Open invoices. Cards are charged from the Open or Overdue tab.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:21.367
Who has a card on file. A 💳 and the last 4 digits next to the customer means a card is on file. Those rows get a tick box on the left.

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:33.933
Charge many at once. 'Select all with a card' ticks them all (or tick rows one by one). 'Charge N cards' charges what's open on each and records card payments, after asking.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.867
Or one invoice. Open the invoice to charge just that one.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:50.833
Charge card. With a card on file and money open, 'Charge card ••1234' shows here. It charges what's still open and records it as a card payment, after asking.

00:00:51.333 --> 00:01:04.000
Card declined. Declined at the terminal or in the batch? Card declined: note what the processor said. Record it emails the customer to update the card and puts a call on the office list.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:09.000
Paid by card at the terminal. Record payment, then pick Card.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:20.400
Card and the surcharge. With Card picked, the card fee from Settings (Contract terms) shows as its own surcharge before you record it. Untick it to waive the fee.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.067
Close. The X closes the form without recording anything.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:31.167
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
